1
00:00:00,000 --> 00:00:14,000
Sometimes when making multi-layered clothing, there will be unstable places.

2
00:00:14,000 --> 00:00:21,000
In the clothing in this video, you can see that it is very unstable between the edge and the panel.

3
00:00:21,000 --> 00:00:24,000
For this kind of clothing, we need to use several functions.

4
00:00:24,000 --> 00:00:30,000
Reverse fire, freeze, hardening

5
00:00:30,000 --> 00:00:35,000
To make it easier for each panel, turn on random colors first.

6
00:00:35,000 --> 00:00:42,000
This dress mainly has three panels, a large dress panel and two cross-stitches.

7
00:00:42,000 --> 00:00:47,000
Use the editor to see the relationship between the two panels.

8
00:00:47,000 --> 00:00:52,000
There is a cross-stitch that is all combined with the outer line of the side panel of the dress.

9
00:00:52,000 --> 00:00:57,000
The other panel is on top of these two panels and belongs to the outer structure.

10
00:00:57,000 --> 00:01:03,000
When the clothing is multi-layered, we usually deal with conflicts from the inside to the outside.

11
00:01:03,000 --> 00:01:07,000
So at this time, I chose the most complete cross-stitch and prepared to reverse fire them.

12
00:01:07,000 --> 00:01:14,000
When a panel is reversed, it will no longer participate in the simulation and will not collide with other panels.

13
00:01:17,000 --> 00:01:21,000
There are two options for reverse fire. One is to reverse fire the sewing line and the panel.

14
00:01:21,000 --> 00:01:24,000
The other option is to reverse fire only the panel.

15
00:01:24,000 --> 00:01:27,000
Here, select the panel and the sewing line to reverse fire.

16
00:01:27,000 --> 00:01:33,000
In this way, the sewing line between the panels will not have any effect.

17
00:01:33,000 --> 00:01:40,000
After opening the simulation, you can see that the unstable place before is now stable.

18
00:01:40,000 --> 00:01:46,000
After changing the perspective, you can see that the position of the pleats is very close to the panel and the panel.

19
00:01:46,000 --> 00:01:50,000
When the panel and the panel are very close to each other,

20
00:01:50,000 --> 00:01:57,000
if you use the add function directly to arrange the panel, it may be unstable.

21
00:02:02,000 --> 00:02:06,000
Now the conflict thickness between the panels is 1, which is too close.

22
00:02:06,000 --> 00:02:10,000
Adjusting to 2.5 can make the distance between the panels farther.

23
00:02:13,000 --> 00:02:17,000
Now switch back to the thick texture surface.

24
00:02:17,000 --> 00:02:19,000
Select these panels on the inner layer.

25
00:02:19,000 --> 00:02:24,000
When the panel is hardened, its bending strength will be increased.

26
00:02:24,000 --> 00:02:26,000
The fold of the fabric becomes very large.

27
00:02:26,000 --> 00:02:28,000
The panel will also be opened a little.

28
00:02:28,000 --> 00:02:34,000
After opening, using the add function will be more stable and easier to deal with future problems.

29
00:02:34,000 --> 00:02:36,000
Then you can remove the hardening.

30
00:02:38,000 --> 00:02:46,000
In order to maintain the shape of these panels and keep them in contact with the edge of the outer layer, they still need to be frozen.

31
00:02:46,000 --> 00:02:51,000
You can see that after opening the simulation, these panels will not participate in the simulation.

32
00:02:51,000 --> 00:02:53,000
They will be frozen in the 3D window.

33
00:02:53,000 --> 00:02:56,000
In the 2D window, select the hidden edge.

34
00:02:56,000 --> 00:02:58,000
Then press Shift-Q to display them.

35
00:02:58,000 --> 00:03:02,000
Then restart them.

36
00:03:02,000 --> 00:03:09,000
After restarting, select Add to the outside.

37
00:03:09,000 --> 00:03:13,000
In this way, the panel will automatically move to the outer layer according to the powder line.

38
00:03:16,000 --> 00:03:19,000
Then press Shift-Q to display them.

39
00:03:19,000 --> 00:03:21,000
Then press Shift-Q to display them.

40
00:03:21,000 --> 00:03:23,000
Then press Shift-Q to display them.

41
00:03:23,000 --> 00:03:25,000
Then press Shift-Q to display them.

42
00:03:25,000 --> 00:03:27,000
Then press Shift-Q to display them.

43
00:03:27,000 --> 00:03:33,000
At this time, when the simulation is started, you will find that this edge of the contract will still be unstable.

44
00:03:33,000 --> 00:03:38,000
First, apply layer 1 to this edge without application layer.

45
00:03:38,000 --> 00:03:40,000
After applying layer, simulate.

46
00:03:40,000 --> 00:03:44,000
The high layer will automatically simulate the outer layer of the lower layer.

47
00:03:44,000 --> 00:03:46,000
Unlock the white panel.

48
00:03:46,000 --> 00:03:49,000
Unlock the white panel.

49
00:03:49,000 --> 00:03:54,000
Unlock the white panel.

50
00:03:54,000 --> 00:03:59,000
Change the body to the back to check the earth face of the material.

51
00:03:59,000 --> 00:04:03,000
Once the material is on the surface, the back of the material will be solid black.

52
00:04:03,000 --> 00:04:06,000
zamfind .

53
00:04:06,000 --> 00:04:14,000
Take a look at this area.

54
00:04:14,000 --> 00:04:23,000
This is the problem with this area, so we have to do some processing on it, otherwise it will be more difficult to correctly identify when opening the simulation.

55
00:04:25,000 --> 00:04:32,000
First of all, when these two plates have entered the skirt through the layer to the outer layer, the layer will need to return to zero.

56
00:04:33,000 --> 00:04:38,000
After the layer returns to zero, the simulation will not be as unstable as it was when preserving the layer.

57
00:04:38,000 --> 00:04:44,000
Then we have to process this piece through to the back of the fabric.

58
00:04:46,000 --> 00:04:50,000
First of all, we click on this piece of fabric in the 3D window.

59
00:04:51,000 --> 00:04:55,000
After clicking, a small blue dot will appear in the 3D and 2D windows at the same time.

60
00:04:56,000 --> 00:05:03,000
Then select the selection grid tool, click near the blue dot in the 2D window and drag the mouse to select a part of the grid.

61
00:05:04,000 --> 00:05:08,000
After selecting, click on the selected area again to drag the axis of the positioning ball.

62
00:05:09,000 --> 00:05:12,000
Then click on the selected area to adjust the grid position.

63
00:05:13,000 --> 00:05:20,000
When selecting the grid, try not to select too much at once, so that there will always be penetrations when adjusting with the positioning ball.

64
00:05:21,000 --> 00:05:24,000
For the less selected grid, use the positioning ball to pull them out.

65
00:05:25,000 --> 00:05:31,000
After starting the simulation, the grid that was pulled out will simulate correctly, and then you can deal with the other parts of the grid.

66
00:05:32,000 --> 00:05:39,000
After processing, you can manually drag the edge of the grid to make it fit the inner layer of the skirt.

67
00:05:40,000 --> 00:05:45,000
Now look at this edge of the grid, you will find that the front part is already stable on the outside.

68
00:05:46,000 --> 00:05:48,000
Then we can fix this part first.

69
00:05:49,000 --> 00:05:54,000
Then click on the selection grid tool and select the same tool in the menu.

70
00:05:55,000 --> 00:06:00,000
Whether it is the selection grid or the positioning ball, if it is drawn directly in the 3D window, it will select all visible grids.

71
00:06:01,000 --> 00:06:03,000
Therefore, the one on the back will also be selected.

72
00:06:04,000 --> 00:06:08,000
Therefore, it is recommended to select the grid and add a fixing pin in the 2D window.

73
00:06:09,000 --> 00:06:17,000
When selecting tools, there are two types of comparison and set-up. The former is to select the area of ​​the frame, and the latter is to freely create an area.

74
00:06:18,000 --> 00:06:23,000
After starting the simulation, these areas with the fixing pin will be fixed in the 3D environment.

75
00:06:24,000 --> 00:06:26,000
Then activate the frozen contract edge panel.

76
00:06:26,000 --> 00:06:33,000
We can see that the part where the skirt is placed will be very close. In this case, it is not convenient to adjust the selection grid.

77
00:06:34,000 --> 00:06:40,000
If the contract edge is frozen, there is no way to change the shape of the skirt, and it will always follow the frozen contract edge.

78
00:06:41,000 --> 00:06:43,000
After starting the simulation, the skirt will still be very soft and unstable.

79
00:06:44,000 --> 00:06:49,000
At this time, select all the plates that form the skirt and print them, so that the skirt is larger and the frame is larger.

80
00:06:50,000 --> 00:06:55,000
During this time, you can manually adjust the position, so that there is enough space between the folds.

81
00:06:57,000 --> 00:07:00,000
Then continue to freeze the contract edge to control the overall shape.

82
00:07:01,000 --> 00:07:03,000
Activate the inner panel.

83
00:07:18,000 --> 00:07:23,000
Select the grid in the 2D window and move these grids in the 3D window.

84
00:07:26,000 --> 00:07:39,000
If the grid is still in the previous position after opening the simulation, you can first convert the selected grid to the fixing pin.

85
00:07:40,000 --> 00:07:44,000
Select some grids and move them to the fixing pin.

86
00:07:45,000 --> 00:07:48,000
Then open the simulation and apply the changes.

87
00:07:49,000 --> 00:07:53,000
Then repeat this step. During this time, you must simulate the application changes.

88
00:07:53,000 --> 00:07:56,000
You can see that the last small piece has been stable and worn to the outside.

89
00:07:57,000 --> 00:07:59,000
Then you can delete the fixing pin and start the simulation.

90
00:08:00,000 --> 00:08:04,000
At this time, the entire grid of the contract edge is already on the outside, and it will not be worn in again.

91
00:08:05,000 --> 00:08:08,000
Then you can delete the existing fixing pin before creating it.

92
00:08:09,000 --> 00:08:14,000
Harden the contract edge of this outer layer and attach the skirt to the inner layer.

93
00:08:15,000 --> 00:08:22,000
After the whole is stable, you can move the inner layer contract edge together.

94
00:08:22,000 --> 00:08:25,000
Let's simulate the other side of the contract edge together.

95
00:08:26,000 --> 00:08:31,000
Let's simulate it first. If it is stable, immediately stop the simulation and finish the hardening process.

96
00:08:32,000 --> 00:08:35,000
During the simulation process, you can continuously press the control button to start or stop the simulation.

97
00:08:36,000 --> 00:08:39,000
Continue to simulate. If there is an unstable place, immediately stop the simulation.

98
00:08:41,000 --> 00:08:46,000
Then you can go back to the previous time to stop the simulation and check where the clothing is unstable.

99
00:08:47,000 --> 00:08:50,000
First of all, the conflict thickness of the outer contract edge is not modified to 2.5.

100
00:08:50,000 --> 00:08:53,000
Therefore, when selecting the two black sides, a red line appears.

101
00:08:54,000 --> 00:08:58,000
Therefore, the conflict thickness will be modified to 2.5 and the particle diameter will be reduced to 10.

102
00:08:59,000 --> 00:09:00,000
If you simulate it again, you can see that it is stable.

103
00:09:01,000 --> 00:09:04,000
At this time, there is an unstable place above, so stop the simulation and simulate it again.

104
00:09:05,000 --> 00:09:06,000
It turned out to be temporarily unstable.

105
00:09:07,000 --> 00:09:12,000
In order to prevent further instability, select this version and reduce the particle diameter to 10 and continue to simulate.

106
00:09:20,000 --> 00:09:23,000
In addition, there is a place to deal with.

107
00:09:24,000 --> 00:09:30,000
Now the two contract edges are integrated on the group board, and they are all custom angle properties, which will cause them to collide.

108
00:09:31,000 --> 00:09:37,000
The cross-sectional line between the contract edge and the group board on the lower layer will be integrated on the inner layer of the contract edge.

109
00:09:44,000 --> 00:09:47,000
After integration, the type of cross-sectional line will be changed to Turned.

110
00:09:47,000 --> 00:09:54,000
After changing to Turned, it will be identified as two contract edges overlapping each other, and it will not be easy to have instability.

111
00:09:58,000 --> 00:10:02,000
After stabilization, the particle diameter can be increased to 20, and there will be no instability.

112
00:10:03,000 --> 00:10:08,000
Then you can deal with other unstable places. See you in the next video.

113
